  "claim_limits": [
    "Intermediate Patch IVV only; not full Upgrade IVVQ.",
    "Recognized historical configurations were generated by official packages with disposable keys. This does not reproduce the reporter host or every upgrade chain.",
    "The actual v4.02.8 downloader required private preservation of its exact verified stale download under temporary-file protection. Its unchanged executable was retried.",
    "The original historical updater can return zero despite a printed error. Acceptance uses package state, executable identity and runtime checks.",
    "Interrupted migration used a reversible directory attribute fault. Process-kill and power-loss durability are not claimed.",
    "The supplemental modern owned-manifest profile lacks shared forwarding permissions. Traffic uses three temporary operator rules restricted to the probe destinations; no automatic policy repair is claimed.",
    "The authenticated offline updater case uses the staged signed candidate CLI. The separate first-hop cases use the actual installed historical updater.",
    "An original updater harness comparison failed only on a live set expiry decreasing from 103 to 102. The preserved capture and separate rerun use a comparator that rejects policy changes and expiry extensions.",
    "The isolated LAN profile does not qualify live external feeds, Geo/ASN, HA endurance or all supported native platforms.",
    "No production reporter-host outcome is inferred from these laboratory observations.",
    "The final snapshot baseline was verified after reapplying only the two original append-only history attributes lost by provider restore. File bytes and identities were preserved. Default tmpfs memory sizing differed by four KiB across boots; all mount flags and other baseline checks remained exact."
  ],
